      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Workspaces: add operations widgets",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOperators need a compact view of active agents and pending workspace-widget approvals without switching away from Workspaces. The legacy implementation targeted the removed dashboard stack and mixed in obsolete contracts.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis rebuild adds two least-privilege built-ins to current Workspaces. `builtin:agent-status` maps the existing sessions payload into bounded Busy/Idle status rows. `builtin:approvals` shows only pending custom-widget registry entries and reuses the existing operator-only `workspaces.widget.approve` decision path. It does not expose execution approvals, plugin approvals, a new RPC allowlist, or a broader approval authority.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can see bounded agent activity and explicitly approve or reject pending custom workspace widgets from accessible controls. Empty, loading, malformed, and decision states are rendered explicitly. Non-operators do not gain approval capability.\n\nGenerated locale synchronization remains intentionally separate: the new English source keys require authenticated translation sync for the repository's generated locales. No generated locale was hand-edited or filled with fallback-only output.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Rebuilt on current `main` and current `extensions/workspaces` / Control UI contracts; no legacy dashboard core is carried forward.\n- Focused post-rebase Vitest: 49/49 schema and widget assertions passed.\n- Tests cover strict mapping, row limits, rendering, decision dispatch, and schema registration.\n- Scoped `oxfmt` / `oxlint`: clean.\n- Fresh local autoreview: no actionable findings; correctness confidence 0.91.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n- Known external gate: generated locale parity requires the repository's authenticated translation provider workflow.\n",
